The USB core unanchors URBs before invoking the completion callback, so after a URB completes, it is removed from the anchor list. The callback resubmits the URB without re-anchoring it to `dev->rx_submitted`. Consequently, when `esd_usb_close()` calls `usb_kill_anchored_urbs(&dev->rx_submitted)`, completed and resubmitted URBs are not in the anchor list and are not freed, causing a memory leak.

