+usb_anchor_urb(urb, &dev->rx_submitted);
 err = usb_submit_urb(urb, GFP_ATOMIC);
+if (!err)
+    return;
+
+usb_unanchor_urb(urb);
```
Reason:
By anchoring the URB to `dev->rx_submitted` before submitting it, the URB remains in the anchor list even after completion (the anchor is only removed by `usb_kill_anchored_urbs` or explicit unanchor). If the submission fails, the URB is unanchored to avoid keeping a stale reference. This ensures that all URBs are properly freed when `esd_usb_close()` kills the anchored URBs.

